# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NexMeet client environment
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Local dev ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to the Vite origin, which proxies /api and /socket.io to the
# backend (see vite.config.ts) — so usually NOTHING needs to be set.

# ── Split-origin deployments (Vercel frontend + Render/EC2 backend) ──
# Set these in the Vercel project settings (build-time env vars).
# All three are required on Vercel — there is no same-origin proxy there.
#
# Backend REST API (Render/AWS URL):
# VITE_API_URL=https://nexmeet-server.onrender.com
#
# Socket.IO chat/presence (same backend host, wss://):
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=wss://nexmeet-server.onrender.com
#
# LiveKit signaling (EC2 SFU behind Caddy TLS):
# VITE_LIVEKIT_WS_URL=wss://sfu.yourdomain.com
#
# NOTE: these are baked into the bundle at BUILD time — changing them in
# the Vercel dashboard triggers a rebuild/redeploy automatically.
